Example 1 – same denominator
  Simplify &frac{3}{x} + &frac{5}{x}
  Denominators are the same: x
  Add numerators: 3 + 5 = 8
  Answer: &frac{8}{x}
  &frac{8}{x}
  (When denominators match, simply add the numerators.)

Example 2 – different single-term denominators
  Simplify &frac{2}{x} + &frac{3}{y}
  LCD = xy
  Rewrite: &frac{2y}{xy} + &frac{3x}{xy}
  Combine: &frac{2y + 3x}{xy}
  &frac{2y + 3x}{xy}
  (Multiply each fraction by the other denominator over itself.)

Find a common denominator and simplify.

(a) &frac{1}{x} + &frac{1}{y}
(b) &frac{3}{a} + &frac{2}{b}
(c) &frac{5}{x} − &frac{1}{2x}
(d) &frac{2}{3x} + &frac{1}{x}

Simplify. Write as a single fraction.

(a) &frac{1}{x+1} + &frac{1}{x+2}
(b) &frac{2}{x+3} + &frac{1}{x+1}
(c) &frac{3}{x+4} − &frac{1}{x+2}
(d) &frac{4}{x−1} + &frac{2}{x+3}

Write as a single fraction in simplest form.

(a) &frac{1}{x} + &frac{1}{x+1}
(b) &frac{3}{x+2} − &frac{2}{x−3}
(c) &frac{x}{x+1} − &frac{x}{x+2}
(d) &frac{2}{x−1} + &frac{3}{x+1}
(e) &frac{1}{x} + &frac{1}{x+1} + &frac{1}{x+2}

✓ &frac{1}{x} + &frac{2}{x} = &frac{3}{x}
✗ &frac{1}{x} + &frac{1}{y} = &frac{2}{x+y}
✓ To add fractions with different denominators, find the LCM first
✗ &frac{a}{b} + &frac{c}{d} = &frac{a+c}{b+d}
✓ &frac{3}{x+1} − &frac{1}{x+1} = &frac{2}{x+1}

teacher_sections.content:
Award marks for correct working and final answers.

Same denominator:
  (a) &frac{7}{x}
  (b) &frac{4}{a}
  (c) &frac{6}{x+1}
  (d) &frac{4}{2x} = &frac{2}{x}

Different single-term denominators:
  (a) &frac{y+x}{xy}
  (b) &frac{3b+2a}{ab}
  (c) &frac{10 − 1}{2x} = &frac{9}{2x}
  (d) &frac{2+3}{3x} = &frac{5}{3x}

Linear expression denominators:
  (a) &frac{2x+3}{(x+1)(x+2)}
  (b) &frac{3x+5}{(x+3)(x+1)}
  (c) &frac{2x+2}{(x+4)(x+2)}
  (d) &frac{6x+14}{(x−1)(x+3)}

Harder subtraction:
  (a) &frac{3x+1}{(x+2)(x+1)}
  (b) &frac{2x+14}{(x−2)(x+4)}
  (c) &frac{x² − x + 2}{(x+1)(x−1)}
  (d) &frac{2x+11}{(2x+1)(x+3)}

Mixed algebraic fractions:
  (a) &frac{2x+1}{x(x+1)}
  (b) &frac{x−13}{(x+2)(x−3)}
  (c) &frac{x}{(x+1)(x+2)}
  (d) &frac{5x−1}{(x−1)(x+1)}
  (e) &frac{3x²+6x+2}{x(x+1)(x+2)}
